<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>The Maritime Loop: Nova Scotia, Cape Breton, and New Brunswick</name>
    <description>Our 8-day loop from the Yarmouth ferry: Wolfville, Grand Pré, Parrsboro, Hopewell Rocks (New Brunswick), Baddeck and the full Cabot Trail, Peggy's Cove, Lunenburg, and Shelburne, then back to Yarmouth. As driven in July 2025: 8 days, 7 nights, about 1,340 miles of driving, including the 186 mile Cabot Trail loop. This is our trip report, not professional guidance. Tides, closures, ferry times, and park rules change, so check them before you go. Trail safety notes: https://backpacksandsnax.com/trail-safety.html Photos: Backpacks &amp; Snax, all rights reserved. Route lines and pin locations (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database License (openstreetmap.org/copyright). Routed with OSRM. More trips like this: https://www.instagram.com/backpacksandsnax</description>
