    <Folder>
      <name>Trip Stops</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>The CAT ferry, Yarmouth</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Day 1 and Day 8: The CAT ferry between Bar Harbor, Maine, and Yarmouth, Nova Scotia. Our sailing left Bar Harbor at 3:00pm on Day 1 and left Yarmouth at 9:30am on Day 8. Schedules change every season, so book from The CAT's current timetable.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1899-E65100</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-66.1245,43.8329,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Tattingstone Inn</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Day 1: 1 night in Wolfville. We got in around 9pm after the 2.5 hour drive from Yarmouth. Day 2 morning: the Wolfville Farmers' Market, if it's running.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1603-0097A7</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-64.3739,45.0901,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Luckett Vineyards</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d2-luckett-1.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d2-luckett-2.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d2-luckett-3.jpg" width="400" /><br><br>Day 2: wine tasting and the red phone booth in the vines, looking out over the Minas Basin. Also close by: Tangled Garden, Domaine de Grand Pré, Blue Beach, Benjamin Bridge, and Lightfoot &amp; Wolfville.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1517-880E4F</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value>https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d2-luckett-1.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d2-luckett-2.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d2-luckett-3.jpg</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-64.2957,45.0721,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Gillespie House Inn</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Days 2 and 3: 2 nights in Parrsboro. Day 2: hiking around Parrsboro. Day 3: day trip to Hopewell Rocks (about 2 hours each way), timed around low tide to walk the ocean floor. The tide runs the whole Fundy shore, so check it before you walk out on the beaches.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1603-006064</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-64.3267,45.4078,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Hopewell Rocks Provincial Park</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-hopewell-1.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-hopewell-2.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-hopewell-3.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-hopewell-4.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-hopewell-5.jpg" width="400" /><br><br>Day 3: day trip from Parrsboro, about 2 hours each way, to some of the highest tides on Earth. The ocean floor is open only for a few hours around low tide, and the water comes back fast. Check the day's tide table, follow the posted times and park staff direction, and never head out on a rising tide. The park and its ocean floor access are seasonal, so check that it's open before you drive over. Tide tables: https://www.nbparks.ca/en/parks/33/hopewell-rocks-provincial-park/26/tide-tables or https://www.tides.gc.ca/]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1684-006064</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value>https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-hopewell-1.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-hopewell-2.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-hopewell-3.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-hopewell-4.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-hopewell-5.jpg</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-64.5783,45.8178,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Parrsboro lighthouse and tidal flats</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-parrsboro-1.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-parrsboro-2.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-parrsboro-3.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-parrsboro-4.jpg" width="400" /><br><br>Day 3, afternoon: back from Hopewell and out on the Parrsboro shore. We walked the flats below the lighthouse at low tide, and by evening the water was all the way back in. The tide comes in fast here too, so check the tide table before you head out and keep an eye on your way back.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-photo</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value>https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-parrsboro-1.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-parrsboro-2.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-parrsboro-3.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d3-parrsboro-4.jpg</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-64.3169,45.3876,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Telegraph House</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Days 4 and 5: 2 nights in Baddeck. Day 4: drive in via New Glasgow and Stellarton, about 4 hours. Day 5: the full Cabot Trail loop, clockwise (see the Cabot Trail layer). Dinner back at The Cable Room in-house.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1603-006064</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-60.7525,46.1001,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Skyline Trail boardwalk</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-skyline-1.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-skyline-2.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-skyline-3.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-skyline-4.jpg" width="400" /><br><br>Day 5, morning: the boardwalk at the end of the Skyline Trail, looking down on the Gulf of St. Lawrence and the Cabot Trail winding along the coast. It's in Cape Breton Highlands National Park, so you need a park pass. Check Parks Canada for trail conditions and closures, stay on the boardwalk, and give moose plenty of room. No drones: Parks Canada doesn't allow recreational drone flying in national parks.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-photo</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value>https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-skyline-1.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-skyline-2.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-skyline-3.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-skyline-4.jpg</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-60.9102,46.748,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Ingonish Beach</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-ingonish-1.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-ingonish-2.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-ingonish-3.jpg" width="400" /><br><br>Day 5, afternoon: Ingonish Beach on the east side of the Cabot Trail, with Middle Head and the Keltic Lodge out on the point. The Middle Head Trail runs out along that point if you have the legs. Cold water and real surf, so watch the waves.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-photo</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value>https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-ingonish-1.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-ingonish-2.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d5-ingonish-3.jpg</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-60.3904,46.6495,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Peggy's Cove</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d6-peggys-2.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d6-peggys-3.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d6-peggys-4.jpg" width="400" /><br><br>Day 6: a stop on the drive from Baddeck to Lunenburg. The lighthouse, the fishing village, and a lot of granite to wander. Stay off the black rocks and back from the water's edge. Waves here can run much bigger than the ones before them and have swept people into the sea.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-photo</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value>https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d6-peggys-2.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d6-peggys-3.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d6-peggys-4.jpg</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-63.9187,44.4918,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Lunenburg Arms Hotel</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Day 6: 1 night in Lunenburg. Walk down to the waterfront in the UNESCO-listed Old Town.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1603-006064</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-64.3103,44.3769,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Lunenburg waterfront</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d7-lunenburg-1.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d7-lunenburg-2.jpg" width="400" /><br><img src="https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d7-lunenburg-3.jpg" width="400" /><br><br>Day 7, morning: the red waterfront buildings of Old Town Lunenburg, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, and a schooner heading out under sail.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-photo</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value>https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d7-lunenburg-1.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d7-lunenburg-2.jpg https://backpacksandsnax.shop/map/maritime-loop/photos/maritime-loop-d7-lunenburg-3.jpg</value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-64.312,44.3761,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>The Coopers Inn B&amp;B</name>
        <description><![CDATA[Day 7: 1 night in Shelburne, a quiet harbor town to slow down in before the ferry. Worth a look: The Emerald Light.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1603-006064</styleUrl>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>-65.3244,43.7623,0</coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
    </Folder>
    <Folder>
      <name>The Maritime Loop (driving route)</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>The Maritime Loop (driving route)</name>
        <description>About 1,153 mi through our stops in trip order, including the Hopewell day trip and Peggy's Cove. Route lines and pin locations (c) OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database License (openstreetmap.org/copyright). Routed with OSRM.</description>
        <styleUrl>#line-1267FF-5000-nodesc</styleUrl>
        <LineString>
          <tessellate>1</tessellate>
          <coordinates>
-66.12454,43.8329,0
-66.12359,43.83268,0
-66.12339,43.83303,0
-66.122,43.8332,0
-66.12175,43.83577,0
-66.12107,43.83824,0
-66.11969,43.83809,0
-66.118,43.84372,0
-66.11548,43.84708,0
-66.09923,43.84135,0
